module iasd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6-iowa }

// The Southern District of Iowa's own periods under the joint N.D. and
// S.D. Iowa Local Rules, computed under FRCP 6(a) (LR 1(j)). Every local
// rule is subject to modification by the presiding judge (LR 1(e)). Rules
// that state no period or limit stay out: commencing cases (LR 3), service
// and sealed and in camera documents (LR 5), the form of motions and oral
// argument (LR 7(b)-(d), (i)-(k)), document form (LR 10), signing (LR 11),
// third parties and amended pleadings (LR 14, 15), the form of discovery
// requests (LR 33), interpreters (LR 43), juror contact and civil juries
// (LR 47, 48), jury instructions (LR 51), injunctions (LR 65), registry
// deposits (LR 67), magistrate judges (LR 72, 73), ADR (LR 72B), the
// clerk, records and transcripts (LR 77, 79), lawyers (LR 83), judicial
// conduct (LR 83A), cameras (LR 83C), opening statements (LR 83D) and
// electronic recordings (LR 83F). Periods measured from a deadline rather
// than an event stay in notes: the parties confer on the proposed
// scheduling order and discovery plan at least 14 days before it is due
// (LR 16(a)) and hold the FRCP 26(f) conference at least 21 days before it
// is due (LR 26(d)); the proposed dispositive motion deadline is at least
// 150 days before the proposed ready-for-trial date (LR 16(g)); and the
// clerk dismisses as to a served defendant when neither an answer nor a
// request for other action is filed within 30 days after the answer was
// due, or when a deadline is exceeded by more than 30 days without an
// extension (LR 41(a)(2), (4)). Periods that bind only the court or the
// clerk stay in notes: service not made within 90 days after the complaint
// is filed (LR 41(a)(1), with the plaintiff's 97-day statement declared
// below), the clerk's notice at least 14 days before a LR 41 dismissal (LR
// 41(c)), and taxation by the clerk on or after 21 days after service of
// the AO 133 form (LR 54(a)(1)(E)). The pro hac vice ECF registration (14
// days, LR 83(d)(3)), the attorney discipline periods (LR 83(g), (h)) and
// the 30-day retention of exhibits (LR 83E) are not encoded. LR 26(c)
// restates the 21-day pretrial disclosure period of LR 16A(c), which is
// declared once, under LR 16A(c). The earlier outline's FRCP flow belongs
// to lit/frcp, and its decisions (Bell Atlantic Corp. v. Twombly, Ashcroft
// v. Iqbal, Celotex Corp. v. Catrett, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Inc.,
// Johnson v. Dayton Elec. Mfg. Co., Braden v. Wal-Mart Stores, Inc. and
// Torgerson v. City of Rochester) are FRCP authority not stated in the
// Local Rules; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.  A
// brief: at most 20 pages, the table of contents, table of  authorities
// and signature block not counted, unless the Local Rules  prescribe
// another limit; trial briefs, Social Security merits briefs and  habeas
// briefs are excepted (LR 7(h)).
limit motion-brief { pages <= 20 cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7(h)" } cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7(h)"
/// A reply brief: at most 5 pages (LR 7(g)).
limit reply-brief { pages <= 5 cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7(g)" } cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7(g)"

/// A principal brief in a bankruptcy appeal: at most 20 pages, exclusive
/// of the tables and any statutory addendum (LR 8001(b), modifying FRBP
/// 8015(a)(7)).
limit bankruptcy-principal-brief {
  pages <= 20 cite "S.D. Iowa LR 8001(b)"
} cite "S.D. Iowa LR 8001(b)"

/// A reply brief in a bankruptcy appeal: at most 5 pages (LR 8001(b)).
limit bankruptcy-reply-brief { pages <= 5 cite "S.D. Iowa LR 8001(b)" } cite "S.D. Iowa LR 8001(b)"

/// The complaint is filed, commencing the action (LR 7.1(a), 16(a), 23,
/// 41(a)(1)).
event ComplaintFiled()
/// The complaint is served on a nongovernmental defendant that is not a
/// natural person (LR 7.1(b)).
event ComplaintServed()
/// A motion other than for summary judgment is served with its brief (LR
/// 7(d), (e)).
event MotionServed() paper motion-brief
/// A resistance to a motion is served (LR 7(g)).
event ResistanceServed()
/// The moving party's reply brief is filed (LR 7(g)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-brief
/// The court rules on a motion without waiting for a resistance (LR 7(e)).
event OrderEnteredWithoutResistance()
/// A motion, resistance or reply that with its supporting filings totals
/// more than 100 pages is filed electronically (LR 5A(g)(8), 10(c)(3),
/// 56(f)).
event LongFilingFiled()
/// An administrative record is filed electronically (LR 5A(g)(9)).
event AdministrativeRecordFiled()
/// A lawyer or party receives the notice of electronic filing of a signed
/// document (LR 5A(i)).
event NefReceived()
/// A notice of removal is filed (LR 16(a), 81(b), (c)).
event NoticeOfRemovalFiled()
/// The notice of removal is served (LR 81(d)).
event NoticeOfRemovalServed()
/// The scheduling order and discovery plan is filed (LR 26(a)).
event SchedulingPlanFiled()
/// The final pretrial conference is held (LR 16A).
event FinalPretrialConference()
/// The discovery deadline passes (LR 37(c)).
event DiscoveryDeadline()
/// A default is entered (LR 41(a)(3)).
event DefaultEntered()
/// A party advises the court that the action has been settled (LR 41(b)).
event SettlementAdvised()
/// The clerk's order dismissing a settled case is entered (LR 41(b)).
event SettlementDismissalEntered()
/// Judgment is entered (LR 54(a)(1)(A)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// The AO 133 form is served (LR 54(a)(1)(C)).
event CostFormServed()
/// The circuit court issues its mandate (LR 54(a)(2)).
event MandateIssued()
/// Final judgment is entered in a Social Security benefits case the
/// plaintiff won (LR 54A(b)).
event SocialSecurityJudgmentEntered()
/// An agency's fee determination under 5 U.S.C. § 504 is entered (LR
/// 54A(c)).
event AgencyFeeOrderEntered()
/// A petition for leave to appeal an agency fee determination is served (LR
/// 54A(c)).
event FeePetitionServed()
/// A motion for summary judgment is served (LR 56(a), (b), (g)).
event SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() paper motion-brief
/// The resisting party's statement of additional material facts is served
/// (LR 56(d)).
event AdditionalFactsServed()
/// A magistrate judge's order on a pretrial matter or report and
/// recommendation is served (LR 72A).
event MagistrateRulingServed()
/// Objections to a magistrate judge's ruling are served (LR 72A).
event ObjectionsServed()
/// Jury selection is scheduled to begin (LR 83B(b)).
event JurySelection()
/// A principal brief is filed in an appeal from the bankruptcy court (LR
/// 8001(b)).
event BankruptcyBriefFiled() paper bankruptcy-principal-brief
/// A reply brief is filed in an appeal from the bankruptcy court (LR
/// 8001(b)).
event BankruptcyReplyBriefFiled() paper bankruptcy-reply-brief

/// LR 7.1(a): within 21 days after a civil complaint is filed, each
/// nongovernmental plaintiff that is not a natural person files its
/// disclosure form.
deadline plaintiff-disclosure-period: 21.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7.1(a)"
/// LR 7.1(b): within 30 days after service of a civil complaint on a
/// nongovernmental defendant that is not a natural person, the defendant
/// files its disclosure statement.
deadline defendant-disclosure-period: 30.days after ComplaintServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7.1(b)"
/// LR 7(e): each party resisting a motion files its resistance brief within
/// 14 days after the motion is served; a resistance to a motion for summary
/// judgment follows LR 56.
deadline resistance-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7(e)"
/// LR 7(e): when the court rules on a motion without waiting for a
/// resistance, any party may move for reconsideration within 7 days after
/// the order is entered.
deadline reconsideration-period: 7.days after OrderEnteredWithoutResistance() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7(e)"
/// LR 7(g): the moving party may file a reply brief, not more than 5 pages,
/// within 7 days after a resistance is served, to assert newly decided
/// authority or answer new and unanticipated arguments.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResistanceServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 7(g)"
/// LR 5A(g)(8): within 7 days after an electronically filed motion,
/// resistance or reply totaling more than 100 pages with its supporting
/// filings is filed, the filer delivers a paper copy to the clerk (also LR
/// 10(c)(3), 56(f)).
deadline paper-copy-period: 7.days after LongFilingFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 5A(g)(8)"
/// LR 5A(g)(9): within 7 days after an administrative record is filed
/// electronically, the filer delivers a paper copy to the clerk.
deadline record-copy-period: 7.days after AdministrativeRecordFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 5A(g)(9)"
/// LR 5A(i): a lawyer or party who disputes the authenticity of a signature
/// on an electronically filed document files an objection within 14 days
/// after receiving the NEF; otherwise the signature is presumed authentic.
deadline signature-objection-period: 14.days after NefReceived() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 5A(i)"
/// LR 16(a): within 90 days after the complaint is filed, all attorneys of
/// record and unrepresented parties submit a proposed Rule 16(b) and 26(f)
/// scheduling order and discovery plan, except in the cases LR 16(d) lists.
deadline scheduling-plan-period: 90.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 16(a)"
/// LR 81(b): within 60 days after a notice of removal is filed, counsel
/// submit the proposed scheduling order and discovery plan (also LR 16(a)).
deadline removal-scheduling-plan-period: 60.days after NoticeOfRemovalFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 81(b)"
/// LR 16(h): in an action for judicial review on an administrative record
/// other than a Social Security benefits case, the parties confer and
/// submit a proposed scheduling order within 90 days after the complaint is
/// filed.
deadline judicial-review-schedule-period: 90.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 16(h)"
/// LR 26(a): objections to the initial disclosures or their timing, made at
/// the Rule 26(f) conference, are memorialized in a document filed within
/// 14 days after the scheduling order and discovery plan is filed.
deadline disclosure-objection-period: 14.days after SchedulingPlanFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 26(a)"
/// LR 16A(b): the proposed final pretrial order is submitted at least 3
/// days before the final pretrial conference.
deadline proposed-pretrial-order-period: 3.days before FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 16A(b)"
/// LR 16A(c): the FRCP 26(a)(3)(A) and LR 83E disclosures of witnesses and
/// exhibits are served at least 21 days before the final pretrial
/// conference (restated in LR 26(c)).
deadline pretrial-disclosure-period: 21.days before FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 16A(c)"
/// LR 16A(d): trial briefs, proposed voir dire, the statement of the case
/// and proposed jury instructions with a verdict form are filed at least 3
/// days before the final pretrial conference.
deadline pretrial-filings-period: 3.days before FinalPretrialConference() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 16A(d)"
/// LR 23(a): in an action brought as a class or representative action, the
/// party seeking to maintain it moves for certification within 180 days
/// after commencement.
deadline class-certification-period: 180.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 23(a)"
/// LR 23(b): in a derivative action under FRCP 23.1, the plaintiff files
/// its certification of adequate representation within 180 days after
/// commencement.
deadline derivative-certification-period: 180.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 23(b)"
/// LR 23(c): in an action under FRCP 23.2 by or against members of an
/// unincorporated association, the parties bringing it file their
/// certification within 180 days after commencement.
deadline association-certification-period: 180.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 23(c)"
/// LR 37(c): except for good cause shown, motions to compel are filed
/// within 14 days after the discovery deadline.
deadline motion-to-compel-period: 14.days after DiscoveryDeadline() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 37(c)"
/// LR 41(a)(1): where no defendant is served within 90 days after the
/// complaint is filed, the clerk dismisses without prejudice unless the
/// plaintiff files a statement of good cause within 97 days after the
/// complaint is filed.
deadline service-statement-period: 97.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 41(a)(1)"
/// LR 41(a)(3): the clerk dismisses without prejudice where a motion for
/// default judgment under FRCP 55(b) is not made within 30 days after the
/// entry of default, unless the plaintiff advises that further court action
/// is needed first.
deadline default-judgment-motion-period: 30.days after DefaultEntered() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 41(a)(3)"
/// LR 41(b): within 30 days after advising the court that an action has
/// been settled, the parties file the documents required to terminate it.
deadline settlement-papers-period: 30.days after SettlementAdvised() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 41(b)"
/// LR 41(b): either party may move to reinstate a settled case dismissed
/// under LR 41(b) within 60 days after the date of the dismissal order.
deadline reinstatement-period: 60.days after SettlementDismissalEntered() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 41(b)"
/// LR 54(a)(1)(A): within 14 days after entry of judgment, a party entitled
/// to costs files the AO 133 form; failing to file it by then waives
/// taxation of costs.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 54(a)(1)(A)"
/// LR 54(a)(1)(C): a party opposing taxation of costs files a resistance
/// within 14 days after service of the AO 133 form.
deadline costs-resistance-period: 14.days after CostFormServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 54(a)(1)(C)"
/// LR 54(a)(2): costs on appeal taxable in the district court under FRAP
/// 39(e) are waived unless the party entitled to them requests their
/// taxation within 21 days after the mandate issues.
deadline appeal-costs-period: 21.days after MandateIssued() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 54(a)(2)"
/// LR 54A(b): in a Social Security benefits case the plaintiff won, counsel
/// files an EAJA fee application or a certificate that the government's
/// positions were substantially justified within 30 days after entry of
/// final judgment.
deadline social-security-fee-period: 30.days after SocialSecurityJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 54A(b)"
/// LR 54A(c): a petition under 5 U.S.C. § 504(c)(2) for leave to appeal an
/// agency fee determination is filed within 30 days after entry of the
/// agency's order.
deadline agency-fee-petition-period: 30.days after AgencyFeeOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 54A(c)"
/// LR 54A(c): any answer to a petition for leave to appeal an agency fee
/// determination is filed within 30 days after service of the petition.
deadline agency-fee-answer-period: 30.days after FeePetitionServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 54A(c)"
/// LR 56(b): a party resisting a motion for summary judgment files its
/// brief, response to the statement of material facts, statement of
/// additional facts and appendix within 21 days after service of the
/// motion.
deadline summary-judgment-resistance-period: 21.days after SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 56(b)"
/// LR 56(g): a request for relief under FRCP 56(d) is made by separate
/// motion filed within 14 days after service of the motion for summary
/// judgment.
deadline rule-56d-motion-period: 14.days after SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 56(g)"
/// LR 56(d): the moving party replies to the resisting party's statement of
/// additional facts within 7 days after its service.
deadline summary-judgment-reply-period: 7.days after AdditionalFactsServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 56(d)"
/// LR 72A: a party seeking review of a magistrate judge's pretrial order or
/// report and recommendation files specific written objections within 14
/// days after service of the order or report.
deadline magistrate-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateRulingServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 72A"
/// LR 72A: any response to objections to a magistrate judge's ruling is
/// filed within 14 days after service of the objections.
deadline magistrate-objection-response-period: 14.days after ObjectionsServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 72A"
/// LR 81(c): within 21 days after filing a notice of removal, each
/// nongovernmental removing party that is not a natural person files its
/// disclosure statement.
deadline removing-party-disclosure-period: 21.days after NoticeOfRemovalFiled() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 81(c)"
/// LR 81(d): within 30 days after service of the notice of removal, each
/// remaining nongovernmental party that is not a natural person files its
/// disclosure statement.
deadline remaining-party-disclosure-period: 30.days after NoticeOfRemovalServed() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 81(d)"
/// LR 83B(b): when a case set for jury trial settles, the clerk is notified
/// at least 7 days before the day scheduled for jury selection; otherwise
/// juror costs may be assessed, except for good cause.
deadline jury-cost-notice-period: 7.days before JurySelection() counted_by frcp6-iowa cite "S.D. Iowa LR 83B(b)"
